{"word":"browse","ipa":"brauz","persianMeaning":"گیاهان و برگ‌های خوراکی برای حیوانات، مطالعه سریع و بی‌نظم، خریداری کردن و دیدن کالاها بدون خریداری الزامی، چرا کردن در مرتع یا چمنزار","englishDefinition":"n. vegetation (such as young shoots, twigs, and leaves) that is suitable for animals to eat\\nn. reading superficially or at random\\nn. the act of feeding by continual nibbling\\nv. look around casually and randomly, without seeking anything in particular","partOfSpeech":"noun","example":"a deer needs to eat twenty pounds of browse every day","examplePersian":"گوسفندان از برگ‌های درختان در مرتع چرا می‌کنند.","cefrLevel":"C2","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"wordFamily":[],"commonMistakes":"","ieltsRelevance":"High","toeflRelevance":"Medium","greRelevance":"High","tags":["IELTS","offline","ECDICT","cet6","gre","ielts","ky","needs-collocation","CEFR-J"],"source":"ECDICT + Openjam + EnglishToPersianDictionaries; CEFR-J 1.5","sourceLicense":"ECDICT MIT; Openjam MIT; EnglishToPersianDictionaries Apache-2.0; CEFR-J commercial use with attribution","frequencyRank":105794,"examPriority":3}
